From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 18:11:10 -0400
Subject: ui: round 7 -- the row is the page, the rail, Arc's folder and pin
 rows

The operator's six from beta 3 (docs/ARC-ROUND2.md, round 7) and the crash
found while capturing them, across the toolbar, the sidebar, folders and
pins:

- The address row is the page's colour exactly, not blended 85% over the
  window ground (a white page's row came out grey), with one hairline where
  it meets the page; the page starts square under the row, its rounded top
  belonging to the row (toolbar T15, T16).
- The star and the row's other page actions take the bar's contrast colour
  through the ColorProvider, as the toolbar's icons do (T17); the location
  bar sizes to its content while it is not being edited and sits on the
  row's centre, so chip, address and star read as one centred cluster (T18).
- The collapsed rail is centred against the card's edge, gutter included;
  its toggle clears the traffic lights by their own height, which the layout
  now hands the strip, and drops below them on the way out of expand-on-
  hover instead of passing under them (sidebar Y6, Y7).
- Folder rows look like Arc's: a folder glyph that opens with the folder, a
  semibold title, the rows' hover tint on the header (folders F12); a
  Space-pinned row away from its home shows Arc's slash between favicon and
  title, the dot staying for cards and the rail (pins H12).
- Quitting with a folder in the sidebar aborted on a variant: the page-colour
  re-theme ran inside the tab strip's close-all notification and reached a
  folder header whose folder had already left the tree. The re-theme is
  posted one turn after the change and skipped while the window empties, and
  the header gives no folder for a node that is not one (F12).
- Two capture params, space_pin_tabs/N and drift_tabs/N, make a drifted
  Space-pinned row without a pointer.

One patch across features rather than six fixups, as 0013 was for round 5:
every one of those patches has been rewritten by a later one on the same
lines (patches/README.md).

Why: docs/ARC-ROUND2.md round 7, the operator's look at beta 3 (2026-09-05).
Removable when: the sidebar, the page card and the folder rows are rebuilt
on upstream's vertical tabs rather than patched onto them.
